module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ExteriorAlgebraDeterminant
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ExteriorStalkUngraded
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.GradedModuleAbelian
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.StalkFreeCover
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.StalkwiseInvertibleDescent
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SymmetricPresentationExact
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.RingedSpace.StalkFinitePresentation

/-!
# The stalk of the determinant subsheaf is the determinant of the stalk

Let `F` be a sheaf of modules of finite presentation on a ringed space and `det(F) ⊆ ⋀(F)` the
annihilator of the degree-one part, formed degree by degree as in
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ExteriorAlgebraDeterminant`. This file proves

`det(F)_x ≅ det(F_x)`

whenever the stalk `F_x` is a finite projective module over the local ring, where the right-hand
side is the determinant line `ProjectiveDeterminant.module` of that module. This is the step the
source of Stacks Tag 0FJN marks as having details omitted.

## Main definitions

* `SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.wedgeGen`: the product of the exterior
  generator of a local section of `F` with a local section of `⋀ⁿ F`, read in degree `n + 1`.
  Its vanishing along every arrow is the condition defining the exterior annihilator.
* `SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.germWedge`: the germ of a local section of
  `⋀ⁿ F`, carried into the exterior algebra of the stalk by the comparison of Tag 01CH.
* `Stacks.ExteriorAnnihilator.part`: the degree-`n` part of the annihilator of the degree-one
  elements of the exterior algebra of a module.
* `SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.determinantStalkDirectSumEquiv`: the stalk of
  `det(F)` as the direct sum over the degrees of those parts for the stalk.

## Main results

* `SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.germWedge_wedgeGen`: the comparison of
  Tag 01CH is multiplicative in the degree-one variable.
* `SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.mem_range_exteriorAnnihilator_iff`: a germ of
  `⋀ⁿ F` is the germ of an exterior annihilated section exactly when it is annihilated by every
  degree-one element of the exterior algebra of the stalk.
* `Stacks.ExteriorAnnihilator.nonempty_directSum_equiv_projectiveDeterminant`: the determinant
  line of a finite projective module is the direct sum of the degreewise parts of the
  annihilator of its degree-one elements.
* `SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.nonempty_determinantStalkEquiv`, and its
  ringed-space form `nonempty_ringedSpaceDeterminantStalkEquiv` in the same namespace: **the
  stalk of the determinant is the determinant line of the stalk.**
* `SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.determinant_stalk_invertible`: every stalk of
  `det(F)` is an invertible module, for `F` flat of finite presentation.
* `determinant_isInvertible_of_finitePresentationDescent`, in the same namespace: **Tag 0FJN**
  with flatness read on the stalks: for `F` with flat stalks and of finite presentation, `det(F)`
  is invertible provided it is of finite presentation. `determinant_isInvertible_of_isFlat`
  (`StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/DeterminantFinitePresentationFlat.lean`) has
  the same conclusion with flatness taken as `AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFlat`, which is
  what the source assumes, and no hypothesis on `det(F)`; it is the form a caller should prefer.

## Implementation notes

**The shape of the argument.** Two things have to be shown, and both are local at `x`. First,
the comparison of Tag 01CH is multiplicative in the degree-one variable: it is pinned only by
its values on germs of wedges, so the formula is proved by presenting a local section of `⋀ⁿ F`
as a finite combination of ordered products of generators — possible near `x` because the germs
of wedges span `⋀ⁿ(F_x)` and finitely many germs are realised over one neighbourhood — and
evaluating both sides there. Second, forming the annihilator commutes with taking stalks. The
annihilation condition quantifies over all arrows out of the object and all degree-one sections
there, which is not a finite condition; but it is linear in the degree-one factor, and `F` is of
finite presentation, so near `x` it is generated by finitely many sections. Being killed by
those finitely many generators therefore suffices, each of those finitely many conditions holds
on a neighbourhood of `x`, and finitely many neighbourhoods have a common refinement.

**Gradedness on the algebraic side.** The annihilator of the degree-one elements of
`ExteriorAlgebra R M` is a graded submodule: a homogeneous component of an annihilated element
is annihilated, since multiplication by a degree-one element raises the degree by one and the
exterior powers are independent. Together with Tag 0FJA, which identifies the annihilator with
the determinant line of a finite projective module, this expresses the determinant line as the
direct sum of the degreewise annihilators, matching the degreewise construction of `det(F)`.

**Transport along an equality of degrees.** The multiplication of the exterior algebra sends
degrees `1` and `n` to degree `1 + n`, whereas the exterior powers are indexed by `(n : ℤ)` and
the relevant target is degree `(n + 1 : ℕ)`. The two integers are equal but not definitionally
so, which is why `wedgeGen` carries a transport `sectionCast`; its vanishing is equivalent to
the vanishing of the untransported product.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FJN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FJN)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FJA](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FJA)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CH](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CH)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01BN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01BN)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite TopologicalSpace CategoryTheory.Sheaf

universe u v

namespace SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras

variable {X : TopCat.{u}}
  {Osharp : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) CommRingCat.{u}}
  {F : SheafOfModules.{u} (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) Osharp)}

/-! ### Transport of homogeneous local sections along an equality of degrees -/

section DegCast

variable {P : ℤ → SheafOfModules.{u} (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) Osharp)}
  {U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ} {i j : ℤ}

/-- Transport of a local section of `P i` to `P j` along an equality `i = j` of degrees. -/
noncomputable abbrev sectionCast (P : ℤ → SheafOfModules.{u}
      (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) Osharp))
    (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ) (h : i = j) (y : ToType ((P i).val.obj U)) :
    ToType ((P j).val.obj U) :=
  Stacks.degCast (F := fun l : ℤ => ToType ((P l).val.obj U)) h y

/-- A transported section vanishes exactly when the original section does. -/
lemma sectionCast_eq_zero_iff (h : i = j) (y : ToType ((P i).val.obj U)) :
    sectionCast P U h y = 0 ↔ y = 0 := by
  subst h; exact Iff.rfl

/-- Transport along an equality of degrees sends zero to zero. -/
lemma sectionCast_zero (h : i = j) :
    sectionCast P U h (0 : ToType ((P i).val.obj U)) = 0 := by
  subst h; rfl

/-- Transport along an equality of degrees is additive. -/
lemma sectionCast_add (h : i = j) (y z : ToType ((P i).val.obj U)) :
    sectionCast P U h (y + z) = sectionCast P U h y + sectionCast P U h z := by
  subst h; rfl

/-- Transport along an equality of degrees commutes with multiplication by a section of the
structure sheaf. -/
lemma sectionCast_smul (h : i = j) (a : ToType ((toRingCat
      (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) Osharp).obj.obj U))
    (y : ToType ((P i).val.obj U)) :
    sectionCast P U h (a • y) = a • sectionCast P U h y := by
  subst h; rfl

/-- Transport along an equality of degrees commutes with restriction. -/
lemma sectionCast_res {V : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ} (h : i = j) (f : U ⟶ V)
    (y : ToType ((P i).val.obj U)) :
    (P j).val.map f (sectionCast P U h y) = sectionCast P V h ((P i).val.map f y) := by
  subst h; rfl

end DegCast

/-! ### Multiplying a homogeneous section by the generator of a section of `F` -/

section WedgeGen

variable (A : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) F)

/-- The degree of the product of a degree-one and a degree-`n` homogeneous section. -/
lemma one_add_natCast (n : ℕ) : (1 : ℤ) + (n : ℤ) = ((n + 1 : ℕ) : ℤ) := by
  push_cast
  ring

/-- The product of the exterior generator of a local section `m` of `F` with a local section of
`⋀ⁿ F`, read in degree `n + 1`. Its vanishing is the condition defining the exterior
annihilator. -/
noncomputable def wedgeGen (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ) (m : ToType (F.val.obj U))
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U)) :
    ToType ((A.exteriorPower (n + 1)).val.obj U) :=
  sectionCast (fun l : ℤ => A.exterior.piece l) U (one_add_natCast n)
    ((A.exterior.mul 1 (n : ℤ)).app U (A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U m) s)

variable {A}

/-- `wedgeGen n U m s` vanishes exactly when the untransported product of the generator of `m`
with `s` does. -/
lemma wedgeGen_eq_zero_iff (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ) (m : ToType (F.val.obj U))
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U)) :
    A.wedgeGen n U m s = 0 ↔
      (A.exterior.mul 1 (n : ℤ)).app U (A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U m) s = 0 :=
  sectionCast_eq_zero_iff _ _

/-- `wedgeGen` is additive in the section of `⋀ⁿ F`. -/
lemma wedgeGen_add_right (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ) (m : ToType (F.val.obj U))
    (s s' : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U)) :
    A.wedgeGen n U m (s + s') = A.wedgeGen n U m s + A.wedgeGen n U m s' := by
  simp only [wedgeGen, map_add, sectionCast_add]

/-- `wedgeGen` vanishes on the zero section of `⋀ⁿ F`. -/
lemma wedgeGen_zero_right (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ) (m : ToType (F.val.obj U)) :
    A.wedgeGen n U m (0 : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U)) = 0 := by
  simp only [wedgeGen, map_zero, sectionCast_zero]

/-- `wedgeGen` is linear over the structure sheaf in the section of `⋀ⁿ F`. -/
lemma wedgeGen_smul_right (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ) (m : ToType (F.val.obj U))
    (a : ToType ((toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) Osharp).obj.obj U))
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U)) :
    A.wedgeGen n U m (a • s) = a • A.wedgeGen n U m s := by
  simp only [wedgeGen]
  rw [(A.exterior.mul 1 (n : ℤ)).map_smul_right, sectionCast_smul]

/-- `wedgeGen` commutes with finite sums in the section of `⋀ⁿ F`. -/
lemma wedgeGen_sum_right {κ : Type*} (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ)
    (m : ToType (F.val.obj U)) (t : Finset κ)
    (s : κ → ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U)) :
    A.wedgeGen n U m (∑ k ∈ t, s k) = ∑ k ∈ t, A.wedgeGen n U m (s k) := by
  classical
  induction t using Finset.induction with
  | empty => rw [Finset.sum_empty, Finset.sum_empty, wedgeGen_zero_right]
  | insert k t hk ih =>
      rw [Finset.sum_insert hk, Finset.sum_insert hk, wedgeGen_add_right, ih]

/-- `wedgeGen` is additive in the section of `F`. -/
lemma wedgeGen_add_left (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ) (m m' : ToType (F.val.obj U))
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U)) :
    A.wedgeGen n U (m + m') s = A.wedgeGen n U m s + A.wedgeGen n U m' s := by
  simp only [wedgeGen, map_add, AddMonoidHom.add_apply, sectionCast_add]

/-- `wedgeGen` vanishes on the zero section of `F`. -/
lemma wedgeGen_zero_left (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ)
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U)) :
    A.wedgeGen n U (0 : ToType (F.val.obj U)) s = 0 := by
  simp only [wedgeGen, map_zero, AddMonoidHom.zero_apply, sectionCast_zero]

/-- `wedgeGen` is linear over the structure sheaf in the section of `F`. -/
lemma wedgeGen_smul_left (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ)
    (a : ToType ((toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) Osharp).obj.obj U))
    (m : ToType (F.val.obj U)) (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U)) :
    A.wedgeGen n U (a • m) s = a • A.wedgeGen n U m s := by
  have hg : A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (a • m) = a • A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U m :=
    (A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U).hom.map_smul a m
  simp only [wedgeGen]
  rw [hg, (A.exterior.mul 1 (n : ℤ)).map_smul_left, sectionCast_smul]

/-- `wedgeGen` commutes with finite sums in the section of `F`. -/
lemma wedgeGen_sum_left {κ : Type*} (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ) (t : Finset κ)
    (m : κ → ToType (F.val.obj U)) (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj U)) :
    A.wedgeGen n U (∑ k ∈ t, m k) s = ∑ k ∈ t, A.wedgeGen n U (m k) s := by
  classical
  induction t using Finset.induction with
  | empty => rw [Finset.sum_empty, Finset.sum_empty, wedgeGen_zero_left]
  | insert k t hk ih =>
      rw [Finset.sum_insert hk, Finset.sum_insert hk, wedgeGen_add_left, ih]

/-- `wedgeGen` commutes with restriction to a smaller open set. -/
lemma wedgeGen_res {U V : Opens (X : Type u)} (n : ℕ) (f : V ⟶ U)
    (m : ToType (F.val.obj (op U))) (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U))) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)) f (A.wedgeGen n (op U) m s) =
      A.wedgeGen n (op V) (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F f m)
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) f s) := by
  simp only [wedgeGen, Stacks.SheafOfModules.res]
  rw [sectionCast_res, (A.exterior.mul 1 (n : ℤ)).naturality f.op,
    PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply A.exteriorGenerator.val f.op m]

end WedgeGen

/-! ### The stalk of a submodule of a sheaf of modules -/

section SubmoduleStalk

variable {M : SheafOfModules.{u} (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) Osharp)}
  (N : M.Submodule) (x : (X : Type u))

/-- The map on stalks induced by the inclusion of a submodule of a sheaf of modules. -/
noncomputable abbrev submoduleStalkι :
    ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf x) →ₗ[ToType
        (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)]
      ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk M.val.presheaf x) :=
  PresheafOfModules.stalkMapL x N.ι.val

variable {N}

/-- `submoduleStalkι N x` sends the germ of a section of `N` to the germ of that section in the
ambient sheaf. -/
lemma submoduleStalkι_germ (U : Opens (X : Type u)) (hx : x ∈ U)
    (t : ToType (N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf.obj (op U))) :
    submoduleStalkι N x (TopCat.Presheaf.germ N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf U x hx t) =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.val.presheaf U x hx (N.ι.val.app (op U) t) :=
  PresheafOfModules.stalkMapL_germ x N.ι.val U hx t

/-- The inclusion of a submodule of a sheaf of modules is injective on sections. -/
lemma injective_ι_val_app (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ) :
    Function.Injective (N.ι.val.app U) := fun _ _ h => Subtype.val_injective h

/-- The image of a section of a submodule under its inclusion lies in that submodule. -/
lemma ι_val_app_mem (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ)
    (t : ToType (N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf.obj U)) :
    N.ι.val.app U t ∈ N.toSubmodule.obj U :=
  Subtype.property t

/-- The stalk of a submodule of a sheaf of modules injects into the stalk of the ambient sheaf:
a section of the submodule whose germ vanishes already vanishes on a smaller object, and then it
vanishes as a section of the submodule. -/
lemma injective_submoduleStalkι : Function.Injective (submoduleStalkι N x) := by
  refine (injective_iff_map_eq_zero _).mpr fun a ha => ?_
  obtain ⟨U, hx, t, ht⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf a
  rw [← ht] at ha
  have h0 : TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.val.presheaf U x hx (N.ι.val.app (op U) t) = 0 :=
    (submoduleStalkι_germ x U hx t).symm.trans ha
  have hz : TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.val.presheaf U x hx (N.ι.val.app (op U) t) =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.val.presheaf U x hx
        (0 : ToType (M.val.presheaf.obj (op U))) := by
    rw [h0, map_zero]
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, i₁, i₂, he⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.germ_eq M.val.presheaf x hx hx
    (N.ι.val.app (op U) t) 0 hz
  have he0 : M.val.presheaf.map i₂.op (0 : ToType (M.val.presheaf.obj (op U))) =
      (0 : ToType (M.val.presheaf.obj (op W))) := by rw [map_zero]
  have he' : M.val.presheaf.map i₁.op (N.ι.val.app (op U) t) =
      (0 : ToType (M.val.presheaf.obj (op W))) := he.trans he0
  have hnat : N.ι.val.app (op W) (N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf.map i₁.op t) =
      M.val.presheaf.map i₁.op (N.ι.val.app (op U) t) :=
    PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply N.ι.val i₁.op t
  have hz0 : N.ι.val.app (op W) (0 : ToType (N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf.obj (op W))) =
      (0 : ToType (M.val.presheaf.obj (op W))) := rfl
  have hzero : N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf.map i₁.op t = 0 :=
    injective_ι_val_app (op W) (hnat.trans (he'.trans hz0.symm))
  rw [← ht, ← TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf i₁ x hxW t,
    hzero, map_zero]

/-- A germ lies in the range of the stalk of the inclusion exactly when it is the germ of a
section lying in the submodule. -/
lemma mem_range_submoduleStalkι_iff (ξ : ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk M.val.presheaf x)) :
    ξ ∈ LinearMap.range (submoduleStalkι N x) ↔
      ∃ (U : Opens (X : Type u)) (hx : x ∈ U) (t : M.val.obj (op U)),
        t ∈ N.toSubmodule.obj (op U) ∧
          TopCat.Presheaf.germ M.val.presheaf U x hx t = ξ := by
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨a, rfl⟩
    obtain ⟨U, hx, t, ht⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf a
    refine ⟨U, hx, N.ι.val.app (op U) t, ι_val_app_mem (op U) t, ?_⟩
    rw [← ht]
    exact (submoduleStalkι_germ x U hx t).symm
  · rintro ⟨U, hx, t, htN, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨TopCat.Presheaf.germ N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf U x hx
      (show ToType (N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf.obj (op U)) from ⟨t, htN⟩), ?_⟩
    exact submoduleStalkι_germ x U hx _

/-- The stalk of a submodule of a sheaf of modules, as the submodule of germs of its sections
inside the stalk of the ambient sheaf. -/
noncomputable def submoduleStalkEquiv :
    ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk N.toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf x) ≃ₗ[ToType
        (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)]
      LinearMap.range (submoduleStalkι N x) :=
  LinearEquiv.ofInjective _ (injective_submoduleStalkι x)

end SubmoduleStalk

/-! ### The germ of a homogeneous section, read in the exterior algebra of the stalk -/

section StalkFormula

variable (A : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) F)
  (x : (X : Type u))

/-- The germ at `x` of a local section of `⋀ⁿ F`, carried by the comparison of Tag 01CH into
`⋀ⁿ` of the stalk of `F` and then read inside the exterior algebra of the stalk. -/
noncomputable def germWedge (n : ℕ) {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U))) :
    ExteriorAlgebra (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x)) :=
  (A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x (Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower n) x hx s)).1

/-- A local section of `⋀ⁿ F` whose `germWedge` vanishes has vanishing germ. -/
lemma germ_eq_zero_of_germWedge_eq_zero (n : ℕ) {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U))) (hs : A.germWedge x n hx s = 0) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower n) x hx s = 0 := by
  have h : A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower n) x hx s) = 0 := Subtype.ext hs
  exact (A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x).injective
    (h.trans (map_zero (A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x)).symm)

/-- `germWedge` is unchanged by restriction to a smaller neighbourhood of `x`. -/
lemma germWedge_res (n : ℕ) {U V : Opens (X : Type u)} (f : V ⟶ U) (hxV : x ∈ V) (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U))) :
    A.germWedge x n hxV (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) f s) =
      A.germWedge x n hxU s := by
  simp only [germWedge]
  rw [Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ_res x f hxV s]

/-- `germWedge` sends the zero section to zero. -/
lemma germWedge_zero (n : ℕ) {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hx : x ∈ U) :
    A.germWedge x n hx (0 : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U))) = 0 := by
  have h1 : Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower n) x hx
      (0 : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U))) = 0 :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ_zero x hx
  simp only [germWedge]
  rw [h1, map_zero]
  rfl

/-- If the germ of `s` is `ξ`, then `germWedge` of `s` is the image of `ξ` under
`exteriorPowerStalkEquiv`. -/
lemma germWedge_eq_of_germ_eq (n : ℕ) {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U)))
    (ξ : ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (A.exteriorPower n).val.presheaf x))
    (h : Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower n) x hx s = ξ) :
    A.germWedge x n hx s = (A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x ξ).1 := by
  simp only [germWedge]
  rw [h]

/-- `Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ_res` with the membership proof at the larger object given
explicitly, so that it can be used to rewrite. -/
lemma germ_res' {M : SheafOfModules.{u}
      (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) Osharp)}
    {U V : Opens (X : Type u)} (f : V ⟶ U) (hxV : x ∈ V) (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (m : ToType (M.val.obj (op U))) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ M x hxV (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res M f m) =
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ M x hxU m :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ_res x f hxV m

/-- Two local sections with the same germ at `x` have equal restrictions to a neighbourhood of
`x`. -/
private lemma exists_res_eq_of_germ_eq {M : SheafOfModules.{u}
      (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) Osharp)}
    {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hxU : x ∈ U) (s s' : ToType (M.val.obj (op U)))
    (h : Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ M x hxU s = Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ M x hxU s') :
    ∃ (W : Opens (X : Type u)) (f : W ⟶ U) (_ : x ∈ W),
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.res M f s = Stacks.SheafOfModules.res M f s' := by
  obtain ⟨W, hxW, i₁, i₂, he⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.germ_eq M.val.presheaf x hxU hxU _ _ h
  rw [Subsingleton.elim i₂ i₁] at he
  exact ⟨W, i₁, hxW, he⟩

/-- `germWedge` commutes with finite sums. -/
lemma germWedge_sum {κ : Type*} (n : ℕ) {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hx : x ∈ U) (t : Finset κ)
    (s : κ → ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U))) :
    A.germWedge x n hx (∑ k ∈ t, s k) = ∑ k ∈ t, A.germWedge x n hx (s k) := by
  simp only [germWedge]
  rw [Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ_sum x hx t s, map_sum]
  exact AddSubmonoidClass.coe_finsetSum _ t

/-- `germWedge` sends a scalar multiple `a • s` to the germ of `a` times `germWedge` of `s`. -/
lemma germWedge_smul (n : ℕ) {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (a : ToType ((toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) Osharp).obj.obj (op U)))
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U))) :
    A.germWedge x n hx (a • s) =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ Osharp.obj U x hx a • A.germWedge x n hx s := by
  have h1 : Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower n) x hx (a • s) =
      TopCat.Presheaf.germ Osharp.obj U x hx a •
        Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower n) x hx s :=
    PresheafOfModules.germ_smul (A.exteriorPower n).val x U hx a s
  simp only [germWedge]
  rw [h1, map_smul]
  rfl

/-- The germ of an ordered product of generators of local sections of `F` is the wedge of their
germs. This is Tag 01CH read in the ungraded exterior algebra of the stalk. -/
lemma germWedge_homogeneousProd (n : ℕ) {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (v : Fin n → ToType (F.val.obj (op U))) :
    A.germWedge x n hx (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op U) n
        fun i => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op U) (v i)) =
      ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)) n
        fun i => Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ F x hx (v i) := by
  simp only [germWedge]
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg Subtype.val
    (SheafOfModules.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv_germ_homogeneousProd A.exterior
      A.exteriorGenerator A.exterior_isExteriorAlgebra n x U hx v)) ?_
  exact exteriorPower.ιMulti_apply_coe _ n _

/-- The wedge of the generator of `m` with an ordered product of generators is the ordered
product of the generators of `m` followed by the others. -/
lemma wedgeGen_homogeneousProd (n : ℕ) (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ)
    (m : ToType (F.val.obj U)) (v : Fin n → ToType (F.val.obj U)) :
    A.wedgeGen n U m (A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd U n
        fun i => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (v i)) =
      A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd U (n + 1)
        fun i => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U
          ((Fin.cons m v : Fin (n + 1) → ToType (F.val.obj U)) i) := by
  rw [Stacks.GradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd_succ A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra U n
    (one_add_natCast n) fun i => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U
      ((Fin.cons m v : Fin (n + 1) → ToType (F.val.obj U)) i)]
  rfl

/-- Two local sections of `⋀ⁿ F` with equal `germWedge` have equal germs at `x`. -/
lemma germ_eq_of_germWedge_eq (n : ℕ) {U V : Opens (X : Type u)} (hxU : x ∈ U) (hxV : x ∈ V)
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U)))
    (s' : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op V)))
    (h : A.germWedge x n hxU s = A.germWedge x n hxV s') :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower n) x hxU s =
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower n) x hxV s' :=
  (A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x).injective (Subtype.ext h)

/-- The germ of a finite combination of ordered products of generators of local sections of `F`
is the corresponding combination of wedges of germs. -/
lemma germWedge_sum_smul_homogeneousProd (n N : ℕ) {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (c : Fin N → ToType ((toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
      Osharp).obj.obj (op U)))
    (v : Fin N → Fin n → ToType (F.val.obj (op U))) :
    A.germWedge x n hx (∑ i, c i • A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op U) n
        fun j => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op U) (v i j)) =
      ∑ i, TopCat.Presheaf.germ Osharp.obj U x hx (c i) •
        ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)) n
          fun j => Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ F x hx (v i j) := by
  rw [A.germWedge_sum x n hx Finset.univ]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  rw [A.germWedge_smul x n hx (c i) _, A.germWedge_homogeneousProd x n hx (v i)]

/-- Restricting a finite combination of ordered products of generators restricts the scalars and
the sections. -/
lemma res_sum_smul_homogeneousProd (n N : ℕ) {U V : Opens (X : Type u)} (f : V ⟶ U)
    (c : Fin N → ToType ((toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
      Osharp).obj.obj (op U)))
    (v : Fin N → Fin n → ToType (F.val.obj (op U))) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) f
        (∑ i, c i • A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op U) n
          fun j => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op U) (v i j)) =
      ∑ i, Stacks.SheafOfModules.resR _ f (c i) •
        A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op V) n
          fun j => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op V) (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F f (v i j)) := by
  rw [Stacks.SheafOfModules.res_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  rw [Stacks.SheafOfModules.res_smul]
  refine congrArg (fun z => Stacks.SheafOfModules.resR _ f (c i) • z) ?_
  refine Eq.trans (Stacks.GradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd_naturality
    A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra f.op n
    (fun j => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op U) (v i j))) ?_
  exact congrArg (fun z => A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op V) n z)
    (funext fun j => (PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply A.exteriorGenerator.val f.op (v i j)).symm)

/-- Finitely many germs of the structure sheaf and of `F`, as prescribed by a combination of
wedges, are realised by sections over one neighbourhood. -/
lemma exists_germ_sum_smul_homogeneousProd (n N : ℕ) {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (fc : Fin N → ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
    (w : Fin N → Fin n → ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x)) :
    ∃ (W : Opens (X : Type u)) (_ : W ⟶ U) (hxW : x ∈ W)
      (c : Fin N → ToType ((toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
        Osharp).obj.obj (op W)))
      (v : Fin N → Fin n → ToType (F.val.obj (op W))),
      (∀ i, TopCat.Presheaf.germ Osharp.obj W x hxW (c i) = fc i) ∧
        ∀ i j, Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ F x hxW (v i j) = w i j := by
  classical
  choose Uc hUc ac hac using fun i : Fin N => TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq Osharp.obj (fc i)
  choose Uv hUv bv hbv using fun p : Fin N × Fin n =>
    TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq F.val.presheaf (w p.1 p.2)
  obtain ⟨W₀, fW₀, hxW₀, hle⟩ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_nbhd_le' x U hx
    (Sum.elim Uc fun p => Uv p) (by rintro (i | p) <;> [exact hUc i; exact hUv p])
  refine ⟨W₀, fW₀, hxW₀, fun i => Stacks.SheafOfModules.resR _ (homOfLE (hle (Sum.inl i))) (ac i),
    fun i j => Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F (homOfLE (hle (Sum.inr (i, j)))) (bv (i, j)),
    fun i => ?_, fun i j => ?_⟩
  · exact (TopCat.Presheaf.germ_res_apply Osharp.obj (homOfLE (hle (Sum.inl i))) x hxW₀
      (ac i)).trans (hac i)
  · exact (Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ_res x (homOfLE (hle (Sum.inr (i, j)))) hxW₀
      (bv (i, j))).trans (hbv (i, j))

/-- **Near a point, a local section of `⋀ⁿ F` is a finite combination of ordered products of
generators.** The comparison of Tag 01CH identifies its germ with an element of `⋀ⁿ` of the
stalk, which is spanned by wedges of germs; finitely many germs are realised by sections over a
single neighbourhood, and the two sections then agree after one more shrinking. -/
lemma exists_res_eq_sum_homogeneousProd (n : ℕ) {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U))) :
    ∃ (W : Opens (X : Type u)) (f : W ⟶ U) (_ : x ∈ W) (N : ℕ)
      (c : Fin N → ToType ((toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
        Osharp).obj.obj (op W)))
      (v : Fin N → Fin n → ToType (F.val.obj (op W))),
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) f s =
        ∑ i, c i • A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op W) n
          fun j => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op W) (v i j) := by
  classical
  have hy : A.germWedge x n hx s ∈
      Submodule.span (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
        (Set.range (ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti
          (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)) n)) := by
    rw [ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti_span_fixedDegree]
    exact (A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower n) x hx s)).2
  obtain ⟨N, fc, g, hsum⟩ := Submodule.mem_span_set'.mp hy
  choose w hw using fun i : Fin N => (g i).2
  obtain ⟨W₀, fW₀, hxW₀, c, v, hgc, hgv⟩ :=
    exists_germ_sum_smul_homogeneousProd (F := F) x n N hx fc w
  have hgerm : Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower n) x hxW₀
        (∑ i, c i • A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op W₀) n
          fun j => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op W₀) (v i j)) =
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower n) x hxW₀
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) fW₀ s) := by
    refine A.germ_eq_of_germWedge_eq x n hxW₀ hxW₀ _ _ ?_
    rw [A.germWedge_sum_smul_homogeneousProd x n N hxW₀ c v,
      A.germWedge_res x n fW₀ hxW₀ hx s]
    refine Eq.trans (Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_) hsum
    rw [hgc i, ← hw i]
    exact congrArg (fun z => fc i • ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)) n z) (funext fun j => hgv i j)
  obtain ⟨W₁, i₁, hxW₁, hres⟩ := exists_res_eq_of_germ_eq x hxW₀ _ _ hgerm.symm
  refine ⟨W₁, i₁ ≫ fW₀, hxW₁, N, fun i => Stacks.SheafOfModules.resR _ i₁ (c i),
    fun i j => Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F i₁ (v i j), ?_⟩
  rw [← Stacks.SheafOfModules.res_res (A.exteriorPower n) fW₀ i₁ s,
    ← A.res_sum_smul_homogeneousProd n N i₁ c v]
  exact hres

/-- The wedge of a generator with a finite combination of ordered products of generators. -/
lemma wedgeGen_sum_smul_homogeneousProd (n N : ℕ) (U : (Opens (X : Type u))ᵒᵖ)
    (m : ToType (F.val.obj U))
    (c : Fin N → ToType ((toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
      Osharp).obj.obj U))
    (v : Fin N → Fin n → ToType (F.val.obj U)) :
    A.wedgeGen n U m (∑ i, c i • A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd U n
        fun j => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U (v i j)) =
      ∑ i, c i • A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd U (n + 1)
        fun j => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app U
          ((Fin.cons m (v i) : Fin (n + 1) → ToType (F.val.obj U)) j) := by
  rw [wedgeGen_sum_right]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  rw [wedgeGen_smul_right, A.wedgeGen_homogeneousProd n U m (v i)]

/-- A wedge of `n + 1` vectors is the first vector times the wedge of the remaining `n`. -/
private lemma ιMulti_cons {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {M : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (n : ℕ) (μ : M) (w : Fin n → M) :
    ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti R (n + 1) (Fin.cons μ w) =
      ExteriorAlgebra.ι R μ * ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti R n w := by
  have htail : Matrix.vecTail (Fin.cons μ w) = w := by
    funext i
    rfl
  rw [ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti_succ_apply, htail]
  rfl

/-- Multiplying a finite combination on the left distributes over the combination. -/
private lemma mul_sum_smul {R : Type*} [CommRing R] {B : Type*} [Ring B] [Algebra R B]
    {ι : Type*} (t : Finset ι) (a : B) (f : ι → R) (y : ι → B) :
    a * ∑ i ∈ t, f i • y i = ∑ i ∈ t, f i • (a * y i) := by
  rw [Finset.mul_sum]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => mul_smul_comm (f i) a (y i)

/-- **Multiplicativity of the comparison of Tag 01CH in the degree-one variable**, for a
section already presented as a combination of ordered products of generators. -/
lemma germWedge_wedgeGen_sum (n N : ℕ) {W : Opens (X : Type u)} (hxW : x ∈ W)
    (m : ToType (F.val.obj (op W)))
    (c : Fin N → ToType ((toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u))
      Osharp).obj.obj (op W)))
    (v : Fin N → Fin n → ToType (F.val.obj (op W))) :
    A.germWedge x (n + 1) hxW (A.wedgeGen n (op W) m
        (∑ i, c i • A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op W) n
          fun j => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op W) (v i j))) =
      ExteriorAlgebra.ι (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ F x hxW m) *
        A.germWedge x n hxW (∑ i, c i •
          A.exterior.toPresheafGradedAlgebra.homogeneousProd (op W) n
            fun j => A.exteriorGenerator.val.app (op W) (v i j)) := by
  rw [A.wedgeGen_sum_smul_homogeneousProd n N (op W) m c v,
    A.germWedge_sum_smul_homogeneousProd x (n + 1) N hxW c _,
    A.germWedge_sum_smul_homogeneousProd x n N hxW c v, mul_sum_smul]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i _ => ?_
  have hcons : (fun j => Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ F x hxW
        ((Fin.cons m (v i) : Fin (n + 1) → ToType (F.val.obj (op W))) j)) =
      Fin.cons (Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ F x hxW m)
        fun j => Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ F x hxW (v i j) := by
    funext j
    refine Fin.cases ?_ ?_ j
    · rfl
    · exact fun j' => rfl
  rw [hcons, ιMulti_cons]

/-- **Multiplicativity of the comparison of Tag 01CH in the degree-one variable.** The germ of
the product of the exterior generator of a local section `m` of `F` with a local section `s` of
`⋀ⁿ F` is the product, in the exterior algebra of the stalk, of the germ of `m` with the germ
of `s`.

Near `x` the section `s` is a combination of ordered products of generators, on which both sides
are computed by the germ formula of Tag 01CH. -/
theorem germWedge_wedgeGen (n : ℕ) {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hx : x ∈ U)
    (m : ToType (F.val.obj (op U))) (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U))) :
    A.germWedge x (n + 1) hx (A.wedgeGen n (op U) m s) =
      ExteriorAlgebra.ι (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ F x hx m) * A.germWedge x n hx s := by
  obtain ⟨W, f, hxW, N, c, v, hv⟩ := A.exists_res_eq_sum_homogeneousProd x n hx s
  rw [← A.germWedge_res x (n + 1) f hxW hx (A.wedgeGen n (op U) m s), A.wedgeGen_res n f m s,
    ← A.germWedge_res x n f hxW hx s, ← germ_res' (M := F) x f hxW hx m, hv]
  exact A.germWedge_wedgeGen_sum x n N hxW (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F f m) c v

/-! ### The stalk of the exterior annihilator -/

/-- **A section killed by the generators of a local presentation is exterior annihilated.** The
annihilation condition is linear in the degree-one factor, and every local section of `F` is,
after shrinking, a combination of the generators; vanishing of a section of a sheaf is local. -/
lemma isExteriorAnnihilated_of_forall_wedgeGen_eq_zero (n : ℕ)
    (LP : Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalPresentation F x)
    {W : Opens (X : Type u)} (fW : W ⟶ LP.nhd)
    (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op W)))
    (h : ∀ k, A.wedgeGen n (op W) (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F fW (LP.gens k)) s = 0) :
    A.IsExteriorAnnihilated n s := by
  intro V f m
  rw [PresheafOfModules.restrictₛₗ_apply]
  refine (A.wedgeGen_eq_zero_iff n V m _).mp ?_
  have hVW : V.unop ≤ W := f.unop.le
  have hf : (A.exteriorPower n).val.map f s =
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) (homOfLE hVW) s := by
    rw [Subsingleton.elim f (homOfLE hVW).op]
    rfl
  rw [hf]
  refine TopCat.Presheaf.IsSheaf.section_ext
    (F := (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)).val.presheaf) (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)).isSheaf ?_
  intro y hy
  obtain ⟨V', g, hyV', c, hc⟩ := LP.generates (homOfLE hVW ≫ fW) m y hy
  refine ⟨V', g.le, hyV', ?_⟩
  have hzero : (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)).val.presheaf.map (homOfLE g.le).op
      (0 : ToType ((A.exteriorPower (n + 1)).val.obj V)) = 0 :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.res_zero (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)) (homOfLE g.le)
  refine Eq.trans ?_ hzero.symm
  have hstep : (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)).val.presheaf.map (homOfLE g.le).op
        (A.wedgeGen n V m (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) (homOfLE hVW) s)) =
      A.wedgeGen n (op V') (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F g m)
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) (g ≫ homOfLE hVW) s) := by
    rw [Subsingleton.elim (homOfLE g.le) g,
      show (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)).val.presheaf.map g.op
          (A.wedgeGen n V m (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) (homOfLE hVW) s)) =
        Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)) g
          (A.wedgeGen n (op V.unop) m
            (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) (homOfLE hVW) s)) from rfl,
      A.wedgeGen_res n g m _, Stacks.SheafOfModules.res_res]
  rw [hstep, hc, wedgeGen_sum_left]
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun k _ => ?_
  rw [wedgeGen_smul_left]
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (fun z => c k • z) ?_) (smul_zero _)
  refine Eq.trans ?_ (Eq.trans (congrArg
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)) (g ≫ homOfLE hVW)) (h k))
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res_zero (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)) (g ≫ homOfLE hVW)))
  rw [A.wedgeGen_res n (g ≫ homOfLE hVW) (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F fW (LP.gens k)) s,
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.res_res]
  refine congrArg (fun z => A.wedgeGen n (op V') z
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) (g ≫ homOfLE hVW) s)) ?_
  rw [Subsingleton.elim (g ≫ homOfLE hVW ≫ fW) ((g ≫ homOfLE hVW) ≫ fW)]

/-- The germ of an exterior annihilated section is annihilated by every degree-one element of
the exterior algebra of the stalk. -/
lemma mul_germWedge_eq_zero_of_isExteriorAnnihilated (n : ℕ) {U : Opens (X : Type u)}
    (hxU : x ∈ U) (t : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U)))
    (ht : A.IsExteriorAnnihilated n t)
    (μ : ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x)) :
    ExteriorAlgebra.ι (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)) μ *
      A.germWedge x n hxU t = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨V, hxV, m, hm⟩ := TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq F.val.presheaf μ
  obtain ⟨W, fWU, hxW, hle⟩ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_nbhd_le' x U hxU
    (fun _ : Unit => V) (fun _ => hxV)
  have hμ : Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ F x hxW
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F (homOfLE (hle ())) m) = μ :=
    (germ_res' (M := F) x (homOfLE (hle ())) hxW hxV m).trans hm
  have hann : A.wedgeGen n (op W) (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F (homOfLE (hle ())) m)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) fWU t) = 0 :=
    (A.wedgeGen_eq_zero_iff n (op W) _ _).mpr
      (ht (op W) fWU.op (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F (homOfLE (hle ())) m))
  have hgw := A.germWedge_wedgeGen x n hxW
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F (homOfLE (hle ())) m)
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) fWU t)
  rw [hann, A.germWedge_zero x (n + 1) hxW, hμ, A.germWedge_res x n fWU hxW hxU t] at hgw
  exact hgw.symm

/-- The sections killed by the germs of the generators of a local presentation, in the form
`isExteriorAnnihilated_of_forall_wedgeGen_eq_zero` consumes: each of the finitely many conditions
holds on a neighbourhood of `x`, so all of them hold on one. -/
lemma exists_res_wedgeGen_gens_eq_zero [F.IsFinitePresentation] (n : ℕ)
    (LP : Stacks.SheafOfModules.LocalPresentation F x) {U : Opens (X : Type u)} (hxU : x ∈ U)
    (fLP : U ⟶ LP.nhd) (s : ToType ((A.exteriorPower n).val.obj (op U)))
    (hs : ∀ k : LP.Gen, Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)) x hxU
      (A.wedgeGen n (op U) (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F fLP (LP.gens k)) s) = 0) :
    ∃ (W : Opens (X : Type u)) (fW : W ⟶ U) (_ : x ∈ W), ∀ k : LP.Gen,
      A.wedgeGen n (op W) (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F (fW ≫ fLP) (LP.gens k))
        (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) fW s) = 0 := by
  classical
  have hk : ∀ k : LP.Gen, ∃ (Wk : Opens (X : Type u)) (gk : Wk ⟶ U) (_ : x ∈ Wk),
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)) gk
        (A.wedgeGen n (op U) (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res F fLP (LP.gens k)) s) = 0 := by
    intro k
    obtain ⟨W', i₁, hxW', he⟩ := exists_res_eq_of_germ_eq x hxU _ 0
      ((hs k).trans (Stacks.SheafOfModules.germ_zero x hxU).symm)
    exact ⟨W', i₁, hxW', he.trans (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res_zero _ i₁)⟩
  choose Wk gk hxWk hWk using hk
  obtain ⟨W, fW, hxW, hleW⟩ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_nbhd_le' x U hxU Wk hxWk
  refine ⟨W, fW, hxW, fun k => ?_⟩
  rw [← Stacks.SheafOfModules.res_res F fLP fW (LP.gens k),
    ← A.wedgeGen_res n fW _ s, Subsingleton.elim fW (homOfLE (hleW k) ≫ gk k),
    ← Stacks.SheafOfModules.res_res (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)) (gk k) (homOfLE (hleW k)) _,
    hWk k]
  exact Stacks.SheafOfModules.res_zero (A.exteriorPower (n + 1)) (homOfLE (hleW k))

/-- A germ of `⋀ⁿ F` killed by every degree-one element of the exterior algebra of the stalk is
the germ of an exterior annihilated section. -/
lemma mem_range_exteriorAnnihilator_of_forall_mul_eq_zero [F.IsFinitePresentation] (n : ℕ)
    (ξ : ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (A.exteriorPower n).val.presheaf x))
    (hμ : ∀ μ : ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x),
      ExteriorAlgebra.ι (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)) μ *
        (A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x ξ).1 = 0) :
    ξ ∈ LinearMap.range (submoduleStalkι (A.exteriorAnnihilator n) x) := by
  obtain ⟨U₀, hxU₀, s, hgs⟩ :=
    TopCat.Presheaf.exists_germ_eq (A.exteriorPower n).val.presheaf ξ
  obtain ⟨LP⟩ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_localPresentation F x
  obtain ⟨U, fU, hxU, hleU⟩ := Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_nbhd_le' x U₀ hxU₀
    (fun _ : Unit => LP.nhd) (fun _ => LP.mem_nhd)
  have hgw : A.germWedge x n hxU (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) fU s) =
      (A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x ξ).1 :=
    (A.germWedge_res x n fU hxU hxU₀ s).trans
      (A.germWedge_eq_of_germ_eq x n hxU₀ s ξ hgs)
  obtain ⟨W, fW, hxW, hW⟩ := A.exists_res_wedgeGen_gens_eq_zero x n LP hxU (homOfLE (hleU ()))
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) fU s) fun k => by
      refine A.germ_eq_zero_of_germWedge_eq_zero x (n + 1) hxU _ ?_
      rw [A.germWedge_wedgeGen x n hxU _ _, hgw]
      exact hμ _
  refine (mem_range_submoduleStalkι_iff x ξ).mpr ⟨W, hxW,
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) fW
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.res (A.exteriorPower n) fU s), ?_, ?_⟩
  · exact A.isExteriorAnnihilated_of_forall_wedgeGen_eq_zero x n LP
      (fW ≫ homOfLE (hleU ())) _ hW
  · refine Eq.trans ?_ hgs
    exact (germ_res' (M := A.exteriorPower n) x fW hxW hxU _).trans
      (germ_res' (M := A.exteriorPower n) x fU hxU hxU₀ s)

/-- **The stalk of the exterior annihilator is the annihilator in the stalk.** A germ of `⋀ⁿ F`
is the germ of an exterior annihilated section exactly when, read through the comparison of
Tag 01CH, it is killed by every degree-one element of the exterior algebra of the stalk.

The forward direction is the germ formula. For the converse, `F` is of finite presentation, so
near `x` it is generated by finitely many sections; the annihilation condition is linear in the
degree-one factor, so being killed by those finitely many generators suffices, and each of those
finitely many conditions holds on a neighbourhood of `x`. -/
theorem mem_range_exteriorAnnihilator_iff [F.IsFinitePresentation] (n : ℕ)
    (ξ : ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (A.exteriorPower n).val.presheaf x)) :
    ξ ∈ LinearMap.range (submoduleStalkι (A.exteriorAnnihilator n) x) ↔
      ∀ μ : ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x),
        ExteriorAlgebra.ι (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)) μ *
          (A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x ξ).1 = 0 := by
  refine ⟨fun hξ μ => ?_, A.mem_range_exteriorAnnihilator_of_forall_mul_eq_zero x n ξ⟩
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, t, htN, hgt⟩ := (mem_range_submoduleStalkι_iff x ξ).mp hξ
  rw [← A.germWedge_eq_of_germ_eq x n hxU t ξ hgt]
  exact A.mul_germWedge_eq_zero_of_isExteriorAnnihilated x n hxU t htN μ

end StalkFormula

end SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras

/-! ### The exterior annihilator of a module, degree by degree -/

namespace Stacks.ExteriorAnnihilator

/-- The annihilator of the degree-one elements of the exterior algebra of `M`. -/
private def ann (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (M : Type v) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] :
    Submodule R (ExteriorAlgebra R M) :=
  ⨅ m : M, LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.mulLeft R (ExteriorAlgebra.ι R m))

private lemma mem_ann_iff {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    {y : ExteriorAlgebra R M} : y ∈ ann R M ↔ ∀ m : M, ExteriorAlgebra.ι R m * y = 0 := by
  simp only [ann, Submodule.mem_iInf, LinearMap.mem_ker, LinearMap.mulLeft_apply]

/-- The degree-`n` part of the annihilator of the degree-one elements, as a submodule of the
`n`th exterior power. -/
noncomputable def part (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (M : Type v) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    (n : ℕ) : Submodule R (⋀[R]^n M) :=
  (⨅ m : M, LinearMap.ker (LinearMap.mulLeft R (ExteriorAlgebra.ι R m))).comap
    (⋀[R]^n M).subtype

/-- An element of the `n`th exterior power lies in `part R M n` exactly when every degree-one
element of the exterior algebra annihilates it. -/
lemma mem_part_iff {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]
    {n : ℕ} (y : ⋀[R]^n M) :
    y ∈ part R M n ↔ ∀ m : M, ExteriorAlgebra.ι R m * (y : ExteriorAlgebra R M) = 0 := by
  simp only [part, Submodule.mem_comap, Submodule.coe_subtype, Submodule.mem_iInf,
    LinearMap.mem_ker, LinearMap.mulLeft_apply]

section Grading

variable {R : Type u} [CommRing R] {M : Type v} [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]

private lemma ι_mem_one (m : M) : ExteriorAlgebra.ι R m ∈ ⋀[R]^1 M := by
  simpa only [pow_one] using LinearMap.mem_range_self (ExteriorAlgebra.ι R) m

/-- A finite sum of elements of pairwise distinct exterior degrees vanishes only if each
summand does. -/
private lemma eq_zero_of_sum_eq_zero {s : Finset ℕ} {y : ℕ → ExteriorAlgebra R M}
    (hy : ∀ i, y i ∈ ⋀[R]^(1 + i) M) (hs : ∑ i ∈ s, y i = 0) {n : ℕ} (hn : n ∈ s) :
    y n = 0 := by
  classical
  have hindep : iSupIndep (fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M) :=
    (DirectSum.Decomposition.isInternal (fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M)).submodule_iSupIndep
  have hmem : y n ∈ ⨆ (j : ℕ) (_ : j ≠ 1 + n), ⋀[R]^j M := by
    have hneg : y n = -∑ i ∈ s.erase n, y i :=
      eq_neg_of_add_eq_zero_left ((Finset.add_sum_erase s y hn).trans hs)
    rw [hneg]
    refine neg_mem (Submodule.sum_mem _ fun i hi => ?_)
    have hin : i ≠ n := Finset.ne_of_mem_erase hi
    exact Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem (1 + i)
      (Submodule.mem_iSup_of_mem (by omega) (hy i))
  exact Submodule.disjoint_def.mp (hindep (1 + n)) _ (hy n) hmem

/-- Every homogeneous component of an element annihilated by the degree-one elements is itself
annihilated by them. -/
private lemma mul_decompose_eq_zero {y : ExteriorAlgebra R M}
    (hy : ∀ m : M, ExteriorAlgebra.ι R m * y = 0) (m : M) (n : ℕ) :
    ExteriorAlgebra.ι R m *
      (DirectSum.decompose (fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M) y n : ExteriorAlgebra R M) = 0 := by
  classical
  by_cases hn : n ∈ (DirectSum.decompose (fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M) y).support
  · refine eq_zero_of_sum_eq_zero
      (y := fun i => ExteriorAlgebra.ι R m *
        (DirectSum.decompose (fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M) y i : ExteriorAlgebra R M))
      (fun i => SetLike.mul_mem_graded (A := fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M) (ι_mem_one m)
        (DirectSum.decompose (fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M) y i).2) ?_ hn
    rw [← Finset.mul_sum, DirectSum.sum_support_decompose]
    exact hy m
  · rw [DFinsupp.notMem_support_iff.mp hn, ZeroMemClass.coe_zero, mul_zero]

end Grading

section Equiv

variable (R : Type u) [CommRing R] (M : Type v) [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]

/-- The sum of the degree-wise inclusions, landing in the exterior algebra. -/
private noncomputable def toExterior :
    (DirectSum ℕ fun n => ↥(part R M n)) →ₗ[R] ExteriorAlgebra R M :=
  (DirectSum.coeLinearMap fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M).comp
    (DirectSum.lmap fun n => (part R M n).subtype)

/-- The sum of the degree-wise inclusions, landing in the annihilator. -/
private noncomputable def toAnn :
    (DirectSum ℕ fun n => ↥(part R M n)) →ₗ[R] ↥(ann R M) :=
  DirectSum.toModule R ℕ _ fun n =>
    LinearMap.restrict (⋀[R]^n M).subtype (p := part R M n) (q := ann R M)
      fun y hy => mem_ann_iff.mpr ((mem_part_iff y).mp hy)

private lemma toExterior_lof (n : ℕ) (y : ↥(part R M n)) :
    toExterior R M (DirectSum.lof R ℕ (fun n => ↥(part R M n)) n y) =
      ((y : ⋀[R]^n M) : ExteriorAlgebra R M) := by
  simp only [toExterior, LinearMap.comp_apply, DirectSum.lmap_lof, DirectSum.coeLinearMap_lof,
    Submodule.coe_subtype]

private lemma coe_toAnn (z : DirectSum ℕ fun n => ↥(part R M n)) :
    ((toAnn R M z : ↥(ann R M)) : ExteriorAlgebra R M) = toExterior R M z := by
  have h : (ann R M).subtype.comp (toAnn R M) = toExterior R M := by
    refine DirectSum.linearMap_ext R fun n => ?_
    refine LinearMap.ext fun y => ?_
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, toAnn, DirectSum.toModule_lof, Submodule.coe_subtype,
      LinearMap.restrict_apply, toExterior_lof]
  simpa only [LinearMap.comp_apply, Submodule.coe_subtype] using DFunLike.congr_fun h z

private lemma toAnn_injective : Function.Injective (toAnn R M) := by
  have hcoe : Function.Injective (toExterior R M) := by
    have h1 : Function.Injective (DirectSum.coeLinearMap fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M) :=
      (DirectSum.Decomposition.isInternal fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M).injective
    have h2 : Function.Injective (DirectSum.lmap fun n => (part R M n).subtype) :=
      (DirectSum.lmap_injective _).mpr fun n => Subtype.val_injective
    exact h1.comp h2
  intro a b hab
  refine hcoe ?_
  rw [← coe_toAnn, ← coe_toAnn, hab]

private lemma toAnn_surjective : Function.Surjective (toAnn R M) := by
  classical
  rintro ⟨y, hy⟩
  have hy' : ∀ m : M, ExteriorAlgebra.ι R m * y = 0 := mem_ann_iff.mp hy
  have hmem : ∀ n : ℕ,
      (DirectSum.decompose (fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M) y n) ∈ part R M n := fun n =>
    (mem_part_iff _).mpr fun m => mul_decompose_eq_zero hy' m n
  refine ⟨∑ n ∈ (DirectSum.decompose (fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M) y).support,
    DirectSum.lof R ℕ (fun n => ↥(part R M n)) n ⟨_, hmem n⟩, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  rw [coe_toAnn, map_sum]
  simp only [toExterior_lof]
  exact DirectSum.sum_support_decompose (fun i : ℕ => ⋀[R]^i M) y

end Equiv

/-- **The determinant line is the direct sum of the degreewise exterior annihilators.** The
annihilator of the degree-one elements is a graded submodule of the exterior algebra, and by
Tag 0FJA it is the determinant line of a finite projective module. -/
theorem nonempty_directSum_equiv_projectiveDeterminant (R : Type u) (M : Type v)
    [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [Module.Finite R M] [Module.Projective R M] :
    Nonempty (DirectSum ℕ (fun n => ↥(part R M n)) ≃ₗ[R]
      ProjectiveDeterminant.module (R := R) (M := M)) :=
  ⟨(LinearEquiv.ofBijective (toAnn R M) ⟨toAnn_injective R M, toAnn_surjective R M⟩).trans
    (LinearEquiv.ofEq _ _ (ProjectiveDeterminant.determinant_submodule_eq_annihilator R M).symm)⟩

end Stacks.ExteriorAnnihilator

/-! ### The stalk of the determinant -/

namespace SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras

variable {X : TopCat.{u}}
  {Osharp : Sheaf (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) CommRingCat.{u}}
  {F : SheafOfModules.{u} (toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) Osharp)}
  (A : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology (X : Type u)) F)
  (x : (X : Type u))

/-- The comparison of Tag 01CH carries the germ of an exterior annihilated section into the
degree-`n` part of the annihilator of the degree-one elements in the exterior algebra of the
stalk. -/
lemma mem_part_of_mem_range [F.IsFinitePresentation] (n : ℕ)
    {ξ : ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (A.exteriorPower n).val.presheaf x)}
    (hξ : ξ ∈ LinearMap.range (submoduleStalkι (A.exteriorAnnihilator n) x)) :
    A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x ξ ∈
      Stacks.ExteriorAnnihilator.part (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x)) n :=
  (Stacks.ExteriorAnnihilator.mem_part_iff _).mpr
    ((A.mem_range_exteriorAnnihilator_iff x n ξ).mp hξ)

/-- **The germs of the exterior annihilated sections are the degree-`n` part of the annihilator
in the stalk**, as a linear equivalence. -/
noncomputable def rangeEquivPart [F.IsFinitePresentation] (n : ℕ) :
    ↥(LinearMap.range (submoduleStalkι (A.exteriorAnnihilator n) x))
      ≃ₗ[ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)]
      ↥(Stacks.ExteriorAnnihilator.part (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x)) n) :=
  LinearEquiv.ofBijective
    (LinearMap.restrict (A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x).toLinearMap
      fun _ hξ => A.mem_part_of_mem_range x n hξ)
    (by
      constructor
      · intro a b hab
        have h := congrArg Subtype.val hab
        simp only [LinearMap.restrict_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe] at h
        exact Subtype.ext ((A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x).injective h)
      · intro y
        refine ⟨⟨(A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x).symm y.1, ?_⟩, ?_⟩
        · refine (A.mem_range_exteriorAnnihilator_iff x n _).mpr fun μ => ?_
          rw [LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply]
          exact (Stacks.ExteriorAnnihilator.mem_part_iff y.1).mp y.2 μ
        · refine Subtype.ext ?_
          simp only [LinearMap.restrict_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe]
          exact (A.exteriorPowerStalkEquiv n x).apply_symm_apply y.1)

/-- **The stalk of the degree-`n` exterior annihilator is the degree-`n` part of the annihilator
in the stalk.** -/
noncomputable def exteriorAnnihilatorStalkEquiv [F.IsFinitePresentation] (n : ℕ) :
    ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (A.exteriorAnnihilator n).toSheafOfModules.val.presheaf x)
      ≃ₗ[ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)]
      Stacks.ExteriorAnnihilator.part (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x)) n :=
  (submoduleStalkEquiv (N := A.exteriorAnnihilator n) x).trans (A.rangeEquivPart x n)

/-- **The stalk of the determinant is the direct sum of the degreewise parts of the annihilator
in the stalk.** The determinant is the direct sum of the degreewise annihilators, and the stalk
of a coproduct is the direct sum of the stalks (Tag 01AH). -/
noncomputable def determinantStalkDirectSumEquiv [F.IsFinitePresentation] :
    ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.determinant.val.presheaf x)
      ≃ₗ[ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)]
      DirectSum ℕ fun n => ↥(Stacks.ExteriorAnnihilator.part
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
        (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x)) n) :=
  (SheafOfModules.natStalkCoprodEquiv
      (fun n : ℕ => (A.exteriorAnnihilator n).toSheafOfModules) x).symm.trans
    (DirectSum.congrLinearEquiv fun n => A.exteriorAnnihilatorStalkEquiv x n)

/-- **The stalk of the determinant subsheaf is the determinant line of the stalk**, for a sheaf
of modules of finite presentation whose stalk at `x` is finite projective. -/
theorem nonempty_determinantStalkEquiv [F.IsFinitePresentation]
    (hfin : Module.Finite (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x)))
    (hproj : Module.Projective (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x))) :
    Nonempty (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk A.determinant.val.presheaf x)
      ≃ₗ[ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x)]
      ProjectiveDeterminant.module
        (R := ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
        (M := ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x))) := by
  have := hfin
  have := hproj
  obtain ⟨e⟩ := Stacks.ExteriorAnnihilator.nonempty_directSum_equiv_projectiveDeterminant
    (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk Osharp.obj x))
    (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk F.val.presheaf x))
  exact ⟨(A.determinantStalkDirectSumEquiv x).trans e⟩

/-! ### The form the determinant lemma on a ringed space consumes -/

section RingedSpace

open AlgebraicGeometry RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

/-- **The stalk of the determinant subsheaf is the determinant of the stalk**, on a ringed
space, in the shape Tag 0FJN consumes: the stalk of `det(F)` at `x` is the determinant line of
the stalk `F_x`, whenever that stalk is finite projective over the local ring.

This is the step the source of Tag 0FJN marks as having details omitted. The module structures
are supplied as `Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkModule`, since the repository carries several
definitionally equal copies between which instance synthesis does not cross. -/
theorem nonempty_ringedSpaceDeterminantStalkEquiv {Y : RingedSpace.{u, u}}
    (G : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing Y)) [G.IsFinitePresentation]
    (A : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier) G) (x : Y)
    (hfin : @Module.Finite _ _ _ _ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkModule G x))
    (hproj : @Module.Projective _ _ _ _ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkModule G x)) :
    Nonempty (@LinearEquiv _ _ _ _ (RingHom.id _) (RingHom.id _) _ _
      (ToType (TopCat.Presheaf.stalk (C := AddCommGrpCat.{u}) A.determinant.val.presheaf x))
      (@ProjectiveDeterminant.module _ _ _ _ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkModule G x)
        hfin hproj) _ _
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkModule A.determinant x) _) :=
  let : SheafOfModules.IsFinitePresentation
      (R := toRingCat (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier) Y.sheaf) G := ‹_›
  A.nonempty_determinantStalkEquiv x hfin hproj

/-- **The stalks of the determinant are invertible modules.** Unconditionally: the stalk of `F`
at `x` is finite projective over the stalk of the structure sheaf, so its determinant line is
invertible by Tag 0FJ9, and `nonempty_ringedSpaceDeterminantStalkEquiv` identifies the stalk of
`det(F)` with that line.

This is as far as the stalks take Tag 0FJN. Invertibility of a sheaf of modules is not a
stalkwise condition — see `Stacks.SheafOfModules.StalkwiseInvertibleDescent` for a sheaf of
modules with invertible stalks that is not invertible — so the passage to `det(F)` itself needs
the finite presentation of `det(F)` as well. -/
theorem determinant_stalk_invertible {Y : RingedSpace.{u, u}}
    (G : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing Y)) [G.IsFinitePresentation]
    (A : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier) G)
    (hflat : ∀ x : Y, @Module.Flat _ _ _ _ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkModule G x)) (x : Y) :
    @Module.Invertible _ _ _ _ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkModule A.determinant x) :=
  stalk_invertible_of_determinantStalkEquiv G A hflat
    (fun x hfin hproj => nonempty_ringedSpaceDeterminantStalkEquiv G A x hfin hproj) x

/-- **The determinant of a sheaf of modules with flat stalks is invertible.** For a sheaf of
modules `F` of finite presentation on a ringed space whose stalks are flat, `det(F)` is an
invertible module provided `det(F)` is of finite presentation ([Stacks, Tag 0FJN], with
flatness read on the stalks).

The finite presentation of `det(F)` cannot be dropped: a sheaf of modules with invertible
stalks need not be invertible (see `Stacks.SheafOfModules.StalkwiseInvertibleDescent`). Nor is
`det(F)` locally free of rank one in general, by
`Stacks.RingedSpace.exists_isInvertible_not_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one`, so the
unconditional clause of Tag 0B8M cannot be used to finish. -/
theorem determinant_isInvertible_of_finitePresentationDescent {Y : RingedSpace.{u, u}}
    (G : SheafOfModules.{u} (structureSheafRing Y)) [G.IsFinitePresentation]
    (A : TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras (Opens.grothendieckTopology Y.carrier) G)
    (hflat : ∀ x : Y, @Module.Flat _ _ _ _ (Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkModule G x))
    (hdet : A.determinant.IsFinitePresentation) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible Y.presheaf
      (Presheaf.isSheaf_comp_of_isSheaf _ Y.presheaf
        (forget₂ CommRingCat.{u} RingCat.{u}) Y.IsSheaf) A.determinant :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.stalkwiseInvertibleDescent Y A.determinant hdet
    (determinant_stalk_invertible G A hflat)

end RingedSpace

end SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras


end
